  "problem": "$$\nf(y,z)=\u27e8\\text{___},\\,y,\\,z\u27e9\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(y,z)$ above parametrizes the parabolic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $8{z}^{2}=x.$ What is the first component of $f?$",
  "worked_solution": "For any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(y,z) & =\u27e8x,y,z\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e88{z}^{2},\\,y,\\,z\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the first component of $f$ is $8{z}^{2}.$",
